hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"209","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman narrated, Shuaib narrated, meaning Ibn Al-Laith, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym Al-Zarqi, on the authority of Asim bin Amr, On the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, he said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until we were in the heat, in the irrigated waters that were To Saad bin Abi Waqqas, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Bring me ablution.” When he performed ablution, he stood up and faced the Qiblah, then said “Allahu Akbar.” Then he said: “My father Abraham, he was your servant and your friend, and he invited you to the people of Mecca, and I, Muhammad, your servant and messenger, invite you to the people of Medina, to “You will bless them in their times and their days, just as you have blessed the people of Mecca, with two blessings.”"
"210","Ibn Abi Dhib said about this story: On the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, performed ablution, then prayed in the land of Saad, and he mentioned the story. “Bundar” and “Muhammad bin Yahya” said: “Uthman bin Omar” said. Ibn Abi Dhib said. Muhammad bin Yahya said, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us"
